{{#if handoff}}## Response contract

Write one JSON document to the handoff file (see Execution) before you finish. Migent reads only that file for the stage result. The response body is a free-form report for humans.

```json
{"schema_version":1,"status":"complete"{{#if decisions}},"decision":"{{decisions.[0].name}}"{{/if}},"summary":"One-line report."}
{"schema_version":1,"status":"blocked","blocker":"What stops you."}{{#if canAsk}}
{"schema_version":1,"status":"question","questions":[{"question":"Which option?","context":"Why you need to know.","selection":"single","recommended":["A"],"options":[{"label":"First choice","description":"Optional detail."},{"label":"Second choice"}]}]}{{/if}}
```

Each line above is a separate example; write exactly one document. `status` is {{statusLabel}}.{{#if decisions}} `decision` is one of {{decisionLabel}}.{{/if}}{{#if canAsk}} `selection` is `single` or `multiple`.{{/if}}

| Status | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| `complete` | The stage's work is finished{{#if artifactName}}, artifact written{{/if}}. `summary` is optional.{{#if decisions}} `decision` is required.{{/if}} |
{{#if canAsk}}| `question` | You need a human answer to continue. |
{{/if}}| `blocked` | An obstacle you cannot resolve in this turn. `blocker` is required. |{{#if decisions}}

## Decisions

Choose exactly one when complete. Set it as `decision` in the handoff file.{{#if canAsk}} Do not choose one while asking a question.{{/if}}
{{#each decisions}}
- `{{name}}`{{#if instruction}}: {{instruction}}{{/if}}{{/each}}{{/if}}{{#if canAsk}}

## Asking questions

Use `status: question` in the handoff file. Keep choices out of the report body.

- Each question needs 2–26 options.
- Omit IDs: Migent letters options A, B, C… and numbers questions 1, 2, 3… in order.
- Optional: `description` on an option; `recommended` on a question, a list of option letters (at most one for `single`).
- Free-text answers are always allowed.
- Several questions are allowed; all must be answered before the stage continues.
- Present choices neutrally. Never decide on the human's behalf.{{/if}}{{else}}## Response contract

Start the response with a status header, then a blank line, then the report:

```
status: {{statusLabel}}{{#if decisions}}
decision: {{decisionLabel}}   ← only with complete{{/if}}
blocker: <reason>   ← only with blocked
```

| Status | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| `complete` | The stage's work is finished{{#if artifactName}}, artifact written{{/if}}. |
{{#if canAsk}}| `question` | You need a human answer to continue. |
{{/if}}| `blocked` | An obstacle you cannot resolve in this turn. |{{#if decisions}}

## Decisions

Choose exactly one when complete. State it in the header, not only in prose.{{#if canAsk}} Do not choose one while asking a question.{{/if}}
{{#each decisions}}
- `{{name}}`{{#if instruction}}: {{instruction}}{{/if}}{{/each}}{{/if}}{{#if canAsk}}

## Asking questions

Write the question document to the question file (see Execution), then return `status: question`. Migent reads the file only for that status. Keep choices out of the report body.

```json
{"schema_version":1,"questions":[{"question":"...","context":"...","selection":"single|multiple","recommended":["A"],"options":[{"label":"...","description":"..."}]}]}
```

- Each question needs 2–26 options.
- Omit IDs: Migent letters options A, B, C… and numbers questions 1, 2, 3… in order.
- Optional: `description` on an option; `recommended` on a question, a list of option letters (at most one for `single`).
- Free-text answers are always allowed.
- Several questions per file are allowed; all must be answered before the stage continues.
- Present choices neutrally. Never decide on the human's behalf.{{/if}}{{/if}}